    "['radius-server group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `radius-server group radius1`:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"group\" concept for RADIUS servers like HUAWEI, but each server is configured individually\\n2. The shared-key is configured as \"secret\" in Juniper\\n3. The source interface\\'s IP (LoopBack0\\'s 192.168.10.1) is configured directly as the source address\\n4. Both authentication and accounting ports are configured on the same server entry', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `radius-server group radius1`:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"group\" concept for RADIUS servers like HUAWEI, but each server is configured individually\\n2. The shared-key is configured as \"secret\" in Juniper\\n3. The source interface\\'s IP (LoopBack0\\'s 192.168.10.1) is configured directly as the source address\\n4. Both authentication and accounting ports are configured on the same server entry', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `radius-server group radius1`:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"group\" concept for RADIUS servers like HUAWEI, but each server is configured individually\\n2. The shared-key is configured as \"secret\" in Juniper\\n3. The source interface\\'s IP (LoopBack0\\'s 192.168.10.1) is configured directly as the source address\\n4. Both authentication and accounting ports are configured on the same server entry', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `radius-server group radius1`:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 source-address 192.168.10.1\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting-port 1813\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"group\" concept for RADIUS servers like HUAWEI, but each server is configured individually\\n2. The shared-key is configured as \"secret\" in Juniper\\n3. The source interface\\'s IP (LoopBack0\\'s 192.168.10.1) is configured directly as the source address\\n4. Both authentication and accounting ports are configured on the same server entry', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 authentication-port 1812'}]]": 1,
    "['radius-server authentication [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 port 1812', 'parent_command': ['set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"'], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here is the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `radius-server authentication` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 port 1812\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper separates the RADIUS server configuration into multiple statements\\n2. The `<key>` should be replaced with the actual shared secret (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s `<key>` placeholder)\\n3. In Juniper, the secret/authentication-key must be configured separately from the server definition\\n4. The port number (1812) is specified directly in the server configuration', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 port 1812'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'parent_command': ['set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"'], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here is the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `radius-server authentication` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 port 1812\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper separates the RADIUS server configuration into multiple statements\\n2. The `<key>` should be replaced with the actual shared secret (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s `<key>` placeholder)\\n3. In Juniper, the secret/authentication-key must be configured separately from the server definition\\n4. The port number (1812) is specified directly in the server configuration', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"'}]]": 1,
    "['radius-server accounting [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting port 1813', 'parent_command': ['set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"'], 'root': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 secret \"<key>\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `radius-server accounting` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting port 1813\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. The command structure uses \"set access radius-server\" instead of \"radius-server accounting\"\\n2. The IP address and port number are specified similarly but with \"accounting port\" syntax\\n3. The shared key would be configured separately in Juniper (not shown here as it wasn\\'t part of the specific command being translated)', 'trans_template': 'set access radius-server 10.20.20.1 accounting port 1813'}]]": 1,
