    "['l2tp-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the Huawei `l2tp-group lns1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols l2tp tunnel lns1\\n##\\n\\nIn Juniper:\\n- The `l2tp-group` in Huawei becomes `tunnel` under the `protocols l2tp` hierarchy in Juniper\\n- The group name `lns1` is preserved as the tunnel identifier\\n- Note that additional parameters like tunnel password would need separate Juniper commands (e.g., `set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1 authentication password`)\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel password cipher [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access l2tp tunnel authentication password \"<password>\"', 'parent_command': ['set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1'], 'root': 'set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `tunnel password cipher <password>`:\\n\\n##\\nset access l2tp tunnel authentication password \"<password>\"\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the L2TP tunnel password is configured under the access hierarchy, and unlike HUAWEI\\'s \"cipher\" option which implies the password is encrypted, Juniper doesn\\'t explicitly mark this in the configuration (though it is securely stored). The angle brackets <password> should be replaced with the actual password value.', 'trans_template': 'set access l2tp tunnel authentication password \"<password>\"'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel name [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access l2tp tunnel lns1 local-name \"LNS\"', 'parent_command': ['set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1'], 'root': 'set protocols l2tp tunnel lns1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI `tunnel name LNS` command:\\n\\n##\\nset access l2tp tunnel lns1 local-name \"LNS\"\\n##\\n\\nThis command sets the local tunnel name to \"LNS\" for the LNS (L2TP Network Server) tunnel configuration in Juniper. The `lns1` identifier corresponds to the HUAWEI\\'s l2tp-group name from the original configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set access l2tp tunnel lns1 local-name \"LNS\"'}]]": 1,
    "['lns-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `lns-group group1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. `set access l2tp lns-group group1` creates the LNS group in Juniper\\n2. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0` binds the source interface (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s LoopBack0)\\n3. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1` binds to the slot/chassis (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s bind slot 1)\\n\\nNote: Juniper uses \"lo0.0\" for loopback interface naming instead of \"LoopBack0\".', 'trans_template': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `lns-group group1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. `set access l2tp lns-group group1` creates the LNS group in Juniper\\n2. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0` binds the source interface (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s LoopBack0)\\n3. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1` binds to the slot/chassis (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s bind slot 1)\\n\\nNote: Juniper uses \"lo0.0\" for loopback interface naming instead of \"LoopBack0\".', 'trans_template': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `lns-group group1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0\\nset access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. `set access l2tp lns-group group1` creates the LNS group in Juniper\\n2. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 interface lo0.0` binds the source interface (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s LoopBack0)\\n3. `set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1` binds to the slot/chassis (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s bind slot 1)\\n\\nNote: Juniper uses \"lo0.0\" for loopback interface naming instead of \"LoopBack0\".', 'trans_template': 'set access l2tp lns-group group1 chassis 1'}]]": 1,
