    "['gateway [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set access address-assignment pool 1 family inet network 192.168.0.2/24', 'parent_command': ['set access address-assignment pool pool1 family inet network 192.168.0.2/24'], 'root': 'set access address-assignment pool pool1 family inet network 192.168.0.2/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Huawei `gateway` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset access address-assignment pool 1 family inet network 192.168.0.2/24\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, the `gateway` command within an IP pool specifies the default gateway and subnet mask for clients\\n- In Juniper, the equivalent is configuring the network under an address-assignment pool, where:\\n  - `192.168.0.2` becomes the network address\\n  - `/24` is the CIDR notation equivalent of 255.255.255.0\\n  - The pool name `1` is maintained from the original configuration\", 'trans_template': 'set access address-assignment pool 1 family inet network 192.168.0.2/24'}]]": 1,
